    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "19th century reform movements arose in response to social stagnation, caste rigidity, gender inequality, and Western liberal thought.",
        "Common methods included scripture reinterpretation, rational critique of idol worship, and establishment of modern schools, journals, and associations.",
        "Major reform movements included Brahmo Samaj, Arya Samaj, Aligarh Movement, and Ramakrishna Mission, each contributing uniquely to social and educational upliftment.",
        "Key legislative and social achievements included the abolition of Sati in 1829, promotion of widow remarriage, and female education.",
        "While foundational for modern Indian nationalism, these movements were largely restricted to the urban middle class and sometimes led to communal differentiation."
      ],
      "id": "pm7ycw1"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The 19th century socio-religious reform movements emerged as a response to social stagnation, religious orthodoxy, caste rigidity, gender inequality, colonial critique, and the impact of Western liberal thought. These movements attempted reinterpretation of religious texts, elimination of social evils, modernization of education, and creation of a rational public sphere.",
      "id": "nfume53"
    },
    {
      "id": "rqxeuab",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2. COMMON FEATURES OF REFORM MOVEMENTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Use of rationalism and reinterpretation of scriptures.",
      "id": "yn8682d"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Critique of idol worship and ritualism (in many movements).",
      "id": "0et2vtk"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Emphasis on women education and widow remarriage.",
      "id": "5pe8ejv"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Attack on caste discrimination (varying intensity).",
      "id": "bj7iten"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Establishment of schools, journals, associations.",
      "id": "5ac9atb"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Creation of middle-class leadership and proto-national consciousness.",
      "id": "4zlil7s"
    },
