      "id": "0yb6fqb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4. BRAHMO SAMAJ — DETAILED ANALYSIS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Founded as Brahma Sabha (1828).",
      "id": "28vr0lq"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Influenced by Upanishads and Unitarianism.",
      "id": "jecm3kl"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Abolition of Sati (1829) during Bentinck’s tenure.",
      "id": "idsercj"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Advocated widow remarriage &amp; women education.",
      "id": "vkqnznj"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Split into Adi Brahmo Samaj (Debendranath Tagore) and Brahmo Samaj of India (Keshab Chandra Sen).",
      "id": "t0a3zmo"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Encouraged modern journalism (Sambad Kaumudi).",
      "id": "k1habzz"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Criticism: limited urban reach.",
      "id": "2wr66sy"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "These movements attempted reinterpretation of religious texts, elimination of social evils, modernization of education, and creation of a rational public sphere.",
      "id": "xyh8fk1"
    },
    {
      "id": "yy7dtxc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5. ARYA SAMAJ — DETAILED ANALYSIS"
    },
