      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Brahmo Samaj split into Adi Brahmo Samaj (led by Debendranath Tagore) and Brahmo Samaj of India (led by Keshab Chandra Sen).",
        "Arya Samaj advocated Vedic infallibility, rejected caste by birth, published Satyarth Prakash, and initiated the Shuddhi reconversion movement.",
        "The Abolition of Sati occurred in 1829 during Lord William Bentinck's tenure, heavily influenced by Brahmo Samaj reforms.",
        "The Aligarh Movement established the Scientific Society (1864) and MAO College, which later became Aligarh Muslim University (AMU) in 1920."
      ],
      "id": "oqn0fb2"
    },
